    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Maintenance-Mechanic_JR103626": {
      "title": "Maintenance Mechanic",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nDepartment Housing & Residence Life Compensation $18.67 to Negotiable Hourly   General Description / Primary Purpose: This position performs skilled maintenance and repair to support the safe, efficient, and continuous operation of campus facilities. The role is responsible for installing, diagnosing, maintaining, and repairing plumbing, electrical, and HVAC systems, as well as performing preventive maintenance on equipment and infrastructure. The incumbent ensures facilities and systems operate in compliance with applicable safety, environmental, and regulatory standards, while responding to service requests and participating in on-call operations to address urgent maintenance needs. Job Functions: Plumbing Install, maintain, alter, and repair sinks, faucets, showers, toilets, urinals, drinking fountains, hot water heaters, valves, etc. Install and repair galvanized, PVC, CPVC & copper pipes for potable water supplies and hot or cold water supply lines for fixtures. Use proper pipe connection procedures, such as soldering copper pipes and fittings and check for leaks. Unstop, repair, replace sanitary drain lines. Operate electric drain routing machine to open drain lines. Electric Install, maintain, alter, repair electrical systems (under & above ground), conduit (underground, exterior & interior), external light fixtures & poles (roadway, parking lot, sidewalk & building), interior light fixtures, power appliances, light machinery, electrical controls (switches, breakers, fuses & panel boxes), transformers, outlets, computer & telephone cables & circuits, etc. Replace ballasts & bulbs in light fixtures. Troubleshoot and repair power & lighting circuits. Refrigeration & Air Conditioning Work Install, maintain, and adjust campus refrigeration air conditioning, heating & ventilation equipment & duct work. Evacuate and recharge air conditioning systems with refrigerants. Remove, overhaul, replace compressors, condensers, etc. Inform supervisor of repair parts & materials needed to be requisitioned. Preventive Maintenance Work Inspect, clean, and replace filters for HVAC units in compliance with EPA certification. Lubricate electric motors. Inspect campus emergency generators, make minor field adjustments & report major malfunctions. Check all elevators. Equipment Operation & Maintenance Possess the ability to properly & safely operate equipment. Check all equipment & vehicles. Follow all established & recommended procedures for the safe & effective operation of equipment. Safety Guidelines Adhere to federal, state, local, campus & departmental safety regulations during the performance of assigned duties. Stay alert for safety violations by other employees that may injure those employees, this employee, or other persons in the area. Report all unsafe situations immediately to supervisor or higher authority. Take immediate action to personally stop unsafe acts if delay to inform supervisor may allow accident to occur. Position will participate in on-call rotation. This position is designated as a Tier 2 respondent for designated campus emergencies and events. In this event of a declared campus emergency, the position incumbent will make every effort to return to campus when directed.   Required Qualifications Completion of an approved apprenticeship program for multiple trades or a high school diploma and 3+ years of relevant experience. Or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/ESL-Instructor_JR103628": {
      "title": "ESL Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nPart time\n\nDepartment English Language Program-OPS Compensation $30.00 Hourly   Job Responsibilities The English Language Program accepts applications on an ongoing basis to maintain a pool of qualified ESL instructors. Instructors are hired as teaching needs arise based on student enrollment, program needs, and instructor availability. Applicants may be contacted when teaching opportunities become available. Employment is offered on a semester-by-semester basis. Job Functions An ESL Instructor provides English language instruction to multilingual and international students at the University of North Florida’s English Language Program. Students come from a variety of countries and linguistic backgrounds and study English for a range of goals, including preparing for university admission and advancing their professional lives. The English Language Program offers six proficiency levels: Beginning 00, High-Beginning 10, Intermediate 20, High-Intermediate 30, Advanced 40, and Pre-University 50. Courses focus primarily on general and academic English, with instruction in reading/writing, listening/speaking/vocabulary, and grammar. The ESL Instructor position is a part-time, in-person position in our Day Program. The Day Program operates Monday–Thursday, 9:00 a.m.–3:00 p.m., for three semesters per year: spring, summer, and fall. A full teaching schedule is 3 classes per day, approximately 26 hours per week. Reduced schedules of 1–2 classes per day may also be available. Instructors indicate their availability when scheduling, and semester assignments are made based on instructor availability, enrollment, and program needs. ESL Instructors are assigned specific courses each semester but should be prepared to teach across subject areas and proficiency levels as program needs require.   Required Qualifications •Bachelor's degree in English, TESOL, Applied Linguistics, Second Language Acquisition, English Education, or a related field. •Experience teaching English to multilingual learners from diverse linguistic and cultural backgrounds. •Knowledge and experience teaching academic English. •Ability to manage a classroom effectively and create an engaging learning environment. ESL Instructors: Prepare and deliver engaging English language lessons using established curriculum materials along with instructor-developed supplemental materials. Teach assigned courses in reading/writing, listening/speaking/vocabulary, and grammar across the program's six proficiency levels. Assess student learning and provide appropriate feedback/academic support to students. Maintain effective classroom management and create a positive, engaging learning environment. Attend faculty meetings and collaborate with instructors within the program. Proctor final examinations. Hold one paid office hour per week. Reading/Writing instructors hold one additional paid tutoring hour per week. Preparation, grading, and other instructional responsibilities are included within the scheduled teaching hours. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in TESOL, Applied Linguistics, Second Language Acquisition, or a related field. Experience teaching ESL/EFL in higher education or university-preparation programs. Experience teaching English abroad.    Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Coordinator-Budgets_JR103579": {
      "title": "Coordinator Budgets",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nDepartment Campus Planning Compensation $45,000.00 to Negotiable Annual   General Description / Primary Purpose The Coordinator Budgets provides budgetary, financial, purchasing, and operational support for Facilities Planning under the direction of department leadership. This position assists with the development, administration, monitoring, and reporting of departmental and project budgets while coordinating purchasing, accounts payable, P-card reconciliation, financial reporting, and related fiscal processes. The Coordinator serves as a key resource to departmental leadership and staff by coordinating financial operations, supporting budget planning activities, producing financial reports, and ensuring compliance with applicable University policies and procedures. Job Functions Budget Administration Administers departmental operating and capital budgets with general oversight form Assistant Director. Advises leadership on budget strategy and internal controls. Exercises authority to approve expenditures within established limits. Develops financial procedures and internal controls. Produce and maintain financial reports utilizing Workday and other financial systems to support operational and budgetary decision-making. Independently analyzes financial trends and recommends corrective action. Coordinate purchasing and accounts payable activities, including direct purchases, invoice processing, and vendor payments. Serve as departmental delegate for P-card holders and coordinate the reconciliation, review, and documentation of transactions. Process revenue reimbursements and other financial transactions. Assist with preparation of required Board of Governors, University, and departmental financial reports. Makes independent determinations regarding financial compliance and fiscal management. Perform budget-related duties as back-up to the Assistant Director of Budgets. Exercise sound judgment in handling confidential financial and personnel information. Office Operations Maintain position descriptions for new, vacant, and existing positions. Coordinate personnel-related documentation and administrative processes within the department. Provide administrative support for special projects, departmental initiatives, meetings, and other activities as assigned. Serve as a resource to departmental staff, vendors, and University stakeholders regarding budget, purchasing, and financial processes. Respond to and resolve inquiries related to financial, purchasing, and operational matters. Coordinate communication and information flow among departmental personnel and campus partners. Support departmental operations through effective coordination of fiscal and administrative activities. Supervisory Responsibilities Supervise assigned OPS employees and/or student assistants. Train, assign, and review work performed by support personnel. Monitor completion of assigned work and provide ongoing guidance and support.   Required Qualifications Master's or Bachelor's degree and 2+ years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.    Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
