    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Industry-Engagement-Manager_JR103608-1": {
      "title": "Industry Engagement Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nDepartment Career Services, Industry Engagement Compensation $50,000.00 Annual   General Description/Primary Purpose: The Industry Engagement Manager primary purpose is responsible for creating, growing and managing relationships with industry partners seeking to develop a recruiting relationship with the University of North Florida. The role is a critical part of the Industry Engagement team, working to craft new career-driven opportunities for UNF students and alumni while regularly communicating directly with industry to ensure needs are met. This position ensures UNF Career Services meets the needs of our employers quickly and accurately with exceedingly high levels of customer service to create strong connections between employers and UNF students, staff, faculty, and alumni. Responsible for managing the connection between UNF and its industry partners. Identifies new prospective employers, manages the relationship of existing employers, and seeks opportunities to grow existing partnerships to better fit the hiring needs of our employers. Oversees the execution of industry relationship initiatives. Job Function: Meets and communicates regularly with employers and community partners, educating on ways to effectively engage, recruit and hire students at the University of North Florida. Works with the whole of the UNF Industry Engagement team to communicate employer needs across colleges and industries. Oversees the relationships of employer partners in dedicated industry fields, partnering with colleges, campus partners and student organizations to ensure that employment opportunities are made widely available for students. Responsible for keeping track of the hiring performance of employer partners and working to ensure that their hiring needs are met while developing new strategies to maintain high levels of employer satisfaction and outstanding customer service. Creates goals for increasing the recruiting presence and performance of industry sectors associated with UNF programs, actively listening to the recruiting needs of the employer community and responding with creative engagement opportunities that meet needs for our students and alumni. Partners with college leadership, faculty, and staff to identify new ways to integrate industry into college programs, curriculum, student organizations and other purposeful means of integration in ways that mutually benefit all stakeholders. Establish customized employer recruiting plans fitting the individual needs of highly engaged employer partners. Grows relationships with recruiting employers and their staff to increase accessibility and awareness of services and opportunities to engage with the university. Advises potential employers and updates current employers on recruiting strategies that will help build their on-campus presence. Optimizes, grows, and tracks employer on-campus engagement strategies with stakeholders. Works with the Associate Director of Industry Engagement and Industry Engagement team to oversee the successful execution of employer events and activities on campus directly related to the industry areas being served by the Industry Engagement Manager. This includes regularly occurring campus recruiting activities such as networking events, industry-focused career fairs, and other university recruiting initiatives. Engages with Student Engagement Team to educate student-facing staff on employer updates and trends. Works with Student Engagement liaisons for similar colleges or industry areas to effectively promote recruiting events and activities to students and alumni. Engages with professional and student organizations to establish further opportunities for employers to hire students across the campus. Development and implementation of all policies related to functions in Career Services. Marginal Functions: Continue professional development. Meets with industry directly through virtual and in-person means, traveling as needed. Attend and present at regional and national conferences as funds allow. During declared campus emergencies, this position may be required to perform specific job-related duties at a designated off campus location or place of residence. Other duties as assigned Supervision Exercised Supervises Graduate Assistants, Student Employees   Required Qualifications Master's and 1+ years of relevant experience or Bachelor's degree and 3+ years of relevant experience. Or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219. Department Requirements: Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with corporate executives, recruiters, university leadership, faculty, staff, students, and community partners. Demonstrated relationship-management and customer-service skills, including the ability to develop, maintain, and grow professional relationships with external organizations. Strong presentation and public-speaking skills, with the ability to represent the university professionally in meetings, events, presentations, and other external-facing settings. Demonstrated organizational and project-management skills, including the ability to manage multiple employer relationships, projects, events, priorities, and deadlines simultaneously. High level of professionalism, responsiveness, and attention to detail. UNF’s Student Success team offers a high energy, collegial work culture where team members contribute every day to helping students succeed. You will rapidly develop portable, marketable skills, expand connections to other professionals in Higher Education, and enjoy opportunities for mentorship and professional development. Your day-to-day efforts will emphasize self-directed and autonomous work. In addition to being part of a dynamic team, you will also have access to a competitive benefits package https://www.unf.edu/hr/benefits/index.html  including UNF’s  Employee Education Program , which includes up to 6 hours of tuition-free courses each semester. In addition to skill specialization and professional development opportunities in this role, you could potentially earn a doctoral degree in Educational Leadership or a master's degree or certificate in one of UNF’s 75 graduate programs in arts and sciences, business, computing and engineering, education, and health. Apply today to become part of a team that empowers students with knowledge, resources, and opportunities to succeed. The following are required documents that must be uploaded to be considered for this position: Resume Cover Letter   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Assistant-VP-of-Institutional-Research-and-Effectiveness_JR103605": {
      "title": "Assistant VP of Institutional Research and Effectiveness",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nDepartment Institutional Research & Performance Compensation $150,000.00 to Negotiable Annual   Job Functions: Under the direction of the Vice President, this position provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for the Offices of Institutional Research and Institutional Effectiveness. Leadership and Administration Provides oversight for state and federal required reporting as completed by Institutional Research which includes but is not limited to IPEDS and State University Database System (SUDS). Provides leadership for the offices in planning, design, data collection, analysis, interpretation, presentation, and validation of institutional research studies, using the full spectrum of university data to inform university administration. Aligns strategic institutional priorities with organizational capacity and available resources to support effective prioritization. Participates in professional organizations and advisory boards such as the Association for Institutional Research, the Southern Association for Institutional Research, the State University System of Florida Council of Data Administrators, and other relevant national and regional professional organizations to remain apprised of current issues and concerns in the field. Serves on the university Performance Funding Taskforce supporting institutional efforts to increase performance in key areas to include but not limited to retention, progression, graduation, and employment and continuing education outcomes. Assists Vice President with managing office budgets, including planning and monitoring budget expenditures. Data Governance and Integrity Serves in a leadership role in university data governance by chairing the Data Management working group and serving on the Data Governance Council. Establishes and implements university-wide data governance standards and policies. Developing and maintaining processes that promote data integrity and consistency across university data sources. Establishes, maintains, and supports the use of institutional reporting standards, data definitions, and documentation within Institutional Research and Institutional Effectiveness. Provides data literacy training and support to campus stakeholders. Serves as the primary contact with internal audit during the annual Performance Based Funding Data Integrity Audit which is required by state statute. External and Compliance Reporting Maintains and reports data required by state and federal governments, external agencies, and accrediting agencies, including but not limited to the Florida Board of Governors, IPEDS, AAUP, NCAA, CUPA, and U.S. News & World Report. Oversees the full Faculty Activity Reporting (FAR) process, from data collection through final reporting of the data to the Board of Governors. Ensures institutional reporting complies with university policies and state and federal regulations through regular monitoring of new and potential legislation. Research and Analysis Conducts quantitative and qualitative research and analysis to support evidence-based planning and decision-making. Provides oversight for administering, analyzing, and sharing data from designated university surveys coordinated by Institutional Research and Institutional Effectiveness. Conducts policy analysis and benchmarking to ensure optimal university performance and compliance. Data Delivery, Availability, and Accessibility Prepares reports, disseminates, and interprets information, provides advice, and delivers presentations to university administration and other stakeholders. Works closely with the Business Intelligence Team in ITS to ensure that appropriate data is ingested in the Enterprise Data Warehouse for strategic analysis to support university decision making. Maintains and enhances the structure, content, and use of university dashboards and reports. Provides data to internal constituents to support data-informed decision-making, assessment, grant development, and other institutional effectiveness functions. Regularly audits data access report to ensure access to sensitive data is associated with business needs. Institutional Effectiveness Fosters a culture of assessment, accountability, continuous quality improvement, and evidence-based decision-making in support of the University’s institutional effectiveness goals. Marginal Functions Acts on the behalf of the Vice President in their absence to include responding to cabinet and executive level data requests and questions. Serves as the University Data Administrator in the Vice President’s absence. During declared campus emergencies, this position may be required to perform specific job-related duties at a designated off-campus location or place of residence. Supervision Exercised Supervises the Director of Assessment and Assistant Director of Institutional Research as well as up to five institutional research programmers and analysts. This position may also supervise Graduate Assistants, Student Assistants, other OPS personnel, and Contract Employees.   Required Qualifications Master's and 7+ years of relevant experience or Bachelor's degree and 9+ years of relevant experience. Or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Athletics-Academic-Coordinator_JR103587": {
      "title": "Athletics Academic Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nDepartment Athletics, Student Athlete Center for Excellence Compensation $45,000.00 Annual   General Description / Primary Purpose: The academic coordinator will provide holistic academic support and monitor the academic progress of assigned student-athletes from matriculation to graduation and assist with the coordination of assigned academic programs as well as student-athlete development events and initiatives. Job Function: Provides academic support to student-athletes and assists with academic coaching in areas including study skills, time management, organizational skills, and other aspects of student life. Meets regularly with students to monitor academic progress, class attendance, and grades. Communicates student-athletes' academic progress, grade checks and reporting weekly to coaching staff. Provides information to student-athletes and coaches regarding institutional polices, academic requirements and athletic eligibility. Provides assistance in course scheduling, career planning, and other University academic requirements. Serves as a liaison between student-athletes and faculty, academic departments, and professional advisors in the university. Monitors and tracks athletic eligibility and academic progress in collaboration with certifying officer and professional advisors. Participates in the recruiting process by meeting with prospective student-athletes in assigned sports. Assists in the development of student-athlete orientation, career, personal and professional development programs. Performs similar or related duties as assigned or required.   Required Qualifications Master's or Bachelor's degree and 2+ years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.  For more information about this position, please contact Tara Sunquist, tara.sunquist@unf.edu.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator   This position has been designated as a Campus Security Authority (CSA). This position has been designated as a CSA because it involves significant responsibility for student and campus activities and/or responsibility for campus security. As such, any person in this position must report to the University Police Department a crime or an incident that might be a crime that he/she becomes aware of. This position has a reporting requirement because the University believes that responsibility for students, campus activities and/or campus security will make the holder of this position someone members of the University community will see as an authority figure and someone to whom they can seek help. A CSA is not expected to investigate or determine whether a criminal incident actually took place. A CSA ’ s responsibility is a duty to report. All positions designated as CSAs are required to complete an online or in - person training session. For more information concerning training or CSA designations, please contact the Clery Act Compliance Manager at (904) 620-1423 or clery@unf.edu.   The holder of this position is responsible for any NCAA and Atlantic Sun Conference bylaws and guidelines that a member of the UNF Athletic Compliance Department provides in addition to all UNF regulations. The individual must also assure that NCAA, Conference and UNF regulations are followed to the best of their knowledge and any violations thereof are reported to UNF Athletic Compliance. Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/SCOEHS---Leadership--Organization--and-community-Impact--LOCI-Part-Time-Faculty-Adjunct_JR103595-1": {
      "title": "SCOEHS/  Leadership, Organization, and community Impact (LOCI)Part-Time Faculty-Adjunct",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nPart time\n\nDepartment Leadership, Organization, & Community Impact (LOCI), Chair-OPS Compensation Negotiable   Teaching classes in the Department of Leadership, Organization, and community Impact, Chair-OPS  The Number of classes will vary by semester based on the department's needs.  Please upload the following documentation to be considered for this position: Updated CV Unofficial Transcript In addition, be prepared to: send send three letters of recommendation (dated less than three years and with a wet or electronic signature are required), and order an official transcript to be sent to Denise Hester at denise.hester@unf.edu   Department  Leadership, School Counseling & Sport Management Compensation is non-negotiable. Equal Opportunity   In 2020, the University of North Florida (UNF) received the prestigious INSIGHT Into Diversity magazine Higher Education Excellence in Diversity (HEED) Award, the only application-based national award for U.S. colleges and universities with outstanding commitment to diversity and inclusion across their campuses. In addition, UNF ranked highest among the HEED institutions and was recognized as a 2020 Diversity Champion.    The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty, and staff from various cultures, backgrounds, and life experiences. The University of North Florida is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment based on genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, gender identity/expression, sexual orientation, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation.  Carnegie     UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens.    Statement(s) of Understanding  This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also need a credit check.  The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator.    Required Qualifications Temporary appointment extended to an expert in a specific field to give instruction in connection with an established program. The appointments are: for one (1) academic term at a time and possess no continuing contractual relationship with the University. May teach undergrad courses with Master's degree in specified discipline. Can be used for temporary (OPS) faculty titles only.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
