    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Residence-Life-Office-Assistant---Student-Employment---Hiring-Operations_JR103661-1": {
      "title": "Residence Life Office Assistant – Student Employment & Hiring Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nDepartment Housing & Residence Life, Residence Life-OPS Compensation $16.25 Hourly   General Description / Primary Purpose The Residence Life Program Assistant – Student Employment & Hiring Operations is responsible for coordinating and maintaining a wide range of administrative and operational functions related to the recruitment, hiring, onboarding, employment maintenance, and separation of student staff within the Department of Housing and Residence Life. This position manages high-volume, cyclical processes with frequently shifting priorities and deadlines, particularly during peak recruitment and transition periods. This role requires exceptional organization, attention to detail, discretion with confidential information, and strong communication skills. The Program Assistant works closely with student staff, professional staff, campus partners, and recruitment and selection committees to ensure accurate, timely, and compliant processing of student employment tasks. Primary systems used include Workday and related university databases, such as Banner, Maxient, StarRez, and erezlife. Housing and Residence Life is an integral part of the University of North Florida and is measured by its ability to support student success through responsive, caring, and effective services. As such, this position requires a positive, self-motivated, service-oriented individual who demonstrates patience, professionalism, and a commitment to equity, accuracy, and collaboration while supporting student staff and professional colleagues. Job Functions / Essential Duties Responsibilities of the Residence Life Program Assistant – Student Employment & Hiring Operations include, but are not limited to: Student Staff Hiring & Employment Administration Coordinate student staff hiring processes from offer through onboarding, including initiation, tracking, and verification of employment actions in Workday. Ensure completion and accuracy of I-9 documentation, onboarding tasks, job changes, rehires, and terminations in accordance with university and federal requirements. Monitor and follow up on incomplete or pending employment actions to ensure timely compliance. Serve as a primary point of contact for student staff regarding employment paperwork, hiring timelines, and Workday-related questions. Recruitment & Selection Support Provide administrative and logistical support for student staff and professional staff recruitment and selection committees. Coordinate hiring timelines, communication templates, tracking tools, and documentation for searches and student staff selection processes. Assist with maintaining accurate recruitment records and employment files in accordance with university retention and confidentiality standards. Timesheets & Payroll Coordination Support student staff timesheet processes, including monitoring submissions, troubleshooting issues, and coordinating corrections as needed. Serve as a liaison between Residence Life, Payroll, and Human Resources to resolve discrepancies or questions related to student employment compensation. Systems, Records, & Data Management Maintain organized, accurate records related to student employment, hiring cycles, and staffing changes. Generate basic reports or tracking documents to support staffing projections, onboarding progress, and audit readiness. Utilize spreadsheets, Microsoft Office tools, Workday, and other institutional systems to support operational needs. Communication & Customer Service Communicate clearly and professionally with student staff, professional staff, and campus partners regarding processes, deadlines, and expectations. Provide high-quality customer service in a fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions and competing priorities. Demonstrate care, patience, and problem-solving skills when supporting students navigating employment processes. Other Duties Participate in move-in, move-out, or peak operational periods as needed to support department-wide priorities. Perform other related duties as assigned to support the mission and operational effectiveness of Housing and Residence Life. Marginal Functions Provide additional staffing support during peak Housing and Residence Life events or operational periods. Assist with special projects related to staffing, hiring process improvements, or departmental initiatives. .   Required Qualifications Preferred Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Experience with Workday or similar enterprise HR systems. Familiarity with student employment practices in higher education. Strong organizational skills and ability to manage confidential information. Ability to work independently while maintaining strong collaborative relationships. Commitment to accurate, student-centered service   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Adjunct---English_JR103657-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct - English",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nPart time\n\nDepartment English & World Languages, Chair-OPS Compensation $0.00 Annual     Required Qualifications Temporary appointment extended to an expert in a specific field to give instruction in connection with an established program. The appointments are: for one (1) academic term at a time and possess no continuing contractual relationship with the University. May teach undergrad courses with Master's degree in specified discipline. Can be used for temporary (OPS) faculty titles only. General Description/Primary Purpose:   Part-time adjunct faculty position in the Department of English. Adjunct faculty are employed on a semester-by-semester basis, as needed, and are non-tenure-earning.  Position responsibilities include but are not limited to: Teach assigned course(s) in accordance with the approved syllabus and course schedule  Hold scheduled office hours with frequency and modality as negotiated with the acting program director and department chair.  Working Hours:  Part-time  Work Schedule:  Varies  Supervision Exercised: This is not a supervisory role.  Required Licensure: N/A     Anticipated Start Date : Dependent on semester hired. Compensation : Adjunct faculty are paid a minimum of $1000 per credit hour.  Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in English discipline or closely related field. Preferred Qualifications: Two years of college-level teaching experience.  Additional Application Materials Required:   Applicants should be prepared to provide the following required documents:  Current curriculum vitae   Cover letter   Names, phone numbers, and email address of three professional references will be requested during the application review stage. The selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts (and, as applicable, U.S. degree equivalency evaluations) documenting the conferral of their qualifying academic credentials by the date of hire.  Job Posting Close Date: Open until filled. Note: Adjunct postings may close at any time without notice.    How to Apply: Applicants must submit an online application that includes all required application documents. If you have any questions about this position, please contact Dr. David Mac Kinnon at 904-620-2741.    About the Department: For more information about the Department of English and World Languages visit: https://www.unf.edu/coas/english/index.html   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
