    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Senior-Director-of-Development-for-ArtsUNF-and-MOCA-Jacksonville_JR103674-1": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Development for ArtsUNF and MOCA Jacksonville",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nDepartment Engagement & Stewardship Management Compensation $110,000.00 to Negotiable Annual   General Description / Primary Purpose: The Senior Director of Development for ArtsUNF and MOCA Jacksonville leads philanthropic strategy and fundraising for ArtsUNF initiatives and the Museum of Contemporary Art Jacksonville, the University of North Florida's largest arts and cultural component. The position works collaboratively with University Development and Alumni Engagement, ArtsUNF, and MOCA leadership to secure support from individuals, corporations, foundations, government sources, and community partners. The position manages a major-gift portfolio and directs fundraising for annual operations, programs, endowment, capital initiatives, exhibitions, collections, education, and student engagement. The largest portion of effort supports MOCA and its approximately $2.5 million annual operating budget. The position reports administratively through University Development and Alumni Engagement and maintains a collaborative reporting relationship with ArtsUNF and MOCA leadership. Job Functions: Develop and execute a comprehensive fundraising plan for ArtsUNF and MOCA, with primary emphasis on MOCA's annual operating and programmatic needs and alignment with University fundraising priorities. Identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward major-gift prospects and donors, emphasizing gifts of $100,000 or more. Manage a portfolio of approximately 100 or more qualified prospects and conduct five to seven substantive donor or prospect meetings per week. Secure philanthropic support for operations, exhibitions, collections, educational and public programs, student opportunities, endowment, capital needs, and other approved strategic priorities through individual, corporate, foundation, government, sponsorship, planned-giving, and campaign strategies. Prepare and coordinate proposals, grant applications, sponsorship materials, case statements, donor presentations, reports, and stewardship communications in collaboration with appropriate University and Museum partners. Engage University and MOCA leaders, the MOCA Board of Trustees, ArtsUNF advisory groups, faculty, staff, and volunteers in prospect identification, cultivation, solicitation, stewardship, campaign activity, and community advocacy. Coordinate donor engagement and fundraising opportunities associated with exhibitions, programs, special events, and community initiatives, and represent ArtsUNF, MOCA, and the University at donor and professional functions. Oversee donor and prospect data management, revenue tracking, proposal activity, and fundraising metrics to support strategic decision-making, effective stewardship, and compliance with institutional policies and donor requirements. Marginal Functions: Represent ArtsUNF, MOCA, and the University at occasional evening, weekend, off-site, or travel-related donor and community activities. Participate in special campaigns, task forces, or institutional initiatives as assigned when those activities fall outside routine fundraising responsibilities. Perform designated job-related duties during a declared emergency at an assigned off-campus location or place of residence. May serve on the Search & Screen Committee for Director-level and above positions.   Required Qualifications Master's and 8+ years of relevant experience or Bachelor's degree and 10+ years of relevant experience. Or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219. Professional Qualifications Fundraising strategy and major-gift portfolio management Donor cultivation, solicitation, stewardship, and relationship management Persuasive written, verbal, and presentation communication Strategic planning, analytical thinking, financial awareness, and sound judgment Collaboration across University, Museum, board, volunteer, and community stakeholders Discretion, attention to detail, project management, and constituent relationship management system proficiency Required documents to be uploaded: Cover letter Resume   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Nursing-Student-Success-Coach_JR103679": {
      "title": "Nursing Student Success Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nPart time\n\nDepartment Brooks College of Health, Associate Dean Compensation $31,000.00 Annual   General Description / Primary Purpose: The Nursing Student Success Coach leads efforts in NCLEX-RN preparation and identifies students at risk to implement targeted remediation strategies in collaboration with SON Director, Assistant Director, and faculty. Job Functions: Student Support & Retention Provide individualized academic coaching and support to nursing students. Foster a welcoming and inclusive environment that promotes student engagement and well-being. Serve as a liaison between students, faculty, and support services to ensure comprehensive academic support. Academic Monitoring & Intervention Identify students at risk at both the course and program levels using academic performance data and faculty input. Track academic progression and maintain detailed records of at-risk students. Design and implement individualized success and remediation plans in collaboration with faculty. Conduct regular follow-up meetings with students to monitor progress and adjust plans as needed. NCLEX-RN Preparation Coordinate and implement NCLEX-RN preparation strategies, including workshops, practice exams, and review sessions. Monitor student performance on standardized assessments and provide targeted support. Program Development & Coordination Develop and coordinate student success offerings such as tutoring, academic workshops, and peer mentoring. Analyze academic performance trends across the prelicensure program to inform strategic planning and continuous improvement. Collaborate with faculty and administration to enhance curriculum and support services based on data-driven insights. Other duties as assigned by Director of SON and/or other BCH leadership. Marginal Functions: Special projects as assigned by Director of SON. May provide back-up to other staff positions within SON. Supervision Received: Reports to Associate Dean, Brooks College of Health. Will perform independently, guided by written and/or verbal instructions. General guidance and direction. The incumbent establishes procedures for attaining specific goals and objectives in a broad area of work; contact between the employee and supervisor is limited in terms of frequency and matters covered.   Required Qualifications Master's or Bachelor's degree and 2+ years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.  This position requires an active and unencumbered RN or APRN License in FL. Policymaking and/or Interpretation: Interpret University and College Policies related to admissions, progression and graduation. Departmental Requirements: This position requires on campus work (not remote) for 20 hours per week at the UNF. It will also require work at the Simulation Center at the Deerwood campus. Preferred Qualifications: Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders. Clinical nursing experience required. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
