      "title": "Athletics Game Day Table Crew - OPS",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nPart time\n\nDepartment Athletics, Marketing-OPS Compensation $15.00 to Negotiable Hourly   Position Summary The UNF Athletics Game Day Table Crew provides customer service and game-day support at athletic events. Crew members assist with general fan engagement, announcing, and game operations to help ensure a positive experience for student-athletes, fans, alumni, sponsors, and guests. This position is ideal for individuals interested in sports administration, event management, customer service, and athletics operations. Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Strong customer service and communication skills. Ability to interact professionally with diverse groups of fans, student-athletes, coaches, staff, donors, and guests. Dependable, punctual, and able to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to stand for extended periods and lift up to 25 pounds.     Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide excellent customer service and answer questions from event attendees. Help with setup and breakdown of game-day tables, signage, and materials. Distribute promotional items, programs, giveaways, and event information. Report issues, concerns, or customer service needs to supervisors promptly. Perform other game-day operational duties as assigned. Work Schedule Hours are based on UNF Athletics event schedules. Evening, weekend, holiday, and occasional daytime availability is needed. Typical shifts range from 3 to 6 hours depending on the event.   Required Qualifications   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Custodial-Worker_JR103693": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nDepartment Physical Facilities, Custodial Services Compensation $16.00 Hourly   General Description / Primary Purpose: This is work performing housekeeping duties including cleaning restrooms, classrooms, offices, common-use areas, and carpet and tile floors in accordance with the APPA cleaning standards. Job Function: Clean and maintain restrooms, classrooms, offices, kitchens, conference rooms, banquet rooms, large assembly rooms, auditoriums, halls, common areas, stairways, elevators, building entrance areas, windows, doors and display cases. Perform additional floor cleaning and maintenance duties. This position is designated as a Tier 2 respondent for designated campus emergencies and events. In the event of a declared campus emergency, the position incumbent will make every effort to return to campus when directed. Supplementary responsibilities. Special set-up requests Graduations Provides manpower during events Cleans up after events Work orders Receives and delivers supplies Assists other departments as needed Picks up materials from vendors. Supervision Received: The incumbent's work is reviewed by the supervisor for accuracy and to ensure instructions are being followed. Schedule Work Hours: Sunday-Friday 10P-6:30A   Required Qualifications Completion of ninth (9th) grade or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219. Some positions may require possession of a classified driver’s license appropriate to a type of vehicle operated.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
