    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/IT-Project-Manager_JR103726-1": {
      "title": "IT Project Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nDepartment Project & Portfolio Management Office Compensation $65,000.00 to Negotiable Annual   General Description / Primary Purpose The IT Project Manager, under the direction of an Associate Director or above within the Project Management Office (PMO), is responsible for leading and managing all aspects of the project lifecycle from project initiation through project closure. This position serves as a key contributor in the planning, coordination, execution, and delivery of technology and business initiatives that support the strategic goals of the University of North Florida. The IT Project Manager applies established project management methodologies, governance standards, and best practices to ensure successful project outcomes. Responsibilities include leading the planning and implementation of projects of varying size and complexity; facilitating the definition of project scope, goals, objectives, and deliverables; coordinating activities among project teams, university departments, vendors, and stakeholders; and ensuring projects are completed on schedule, within budget, and in alignment with quality expectations and organizational objectives. The IT Project Manager fosters effective communication, collaboration, risk management, and stakeholder engagement throughout the project lifecycle to support successful delivery and institutional effectiveness Job Functions Lead the planning, execution, monitoring, and closure of technology and business projects of varying size and complexity, ensuring alignment with university strategic goals, project objectives, and established project management methodologies. Facilitate the definition of project scope, objectives, deliverables, success criteria, assumptions, constraints, and resource requirements in collaboration with stakeholders, sponsors, functional offices, and technical teams. Develop and maintain comprehensive project management artifacts, including project charters, schedules, work plans, risk registers, communication plans, status reports, and project budgets to support project governance and informed decision-making. Coordinate project activities and resources across multiple departments, project teams, vendors, consultants, and external partners to ensure project milestones and deliverables are completed on schedule, within budget, and in accordance with quality standards. Monitor and control project performance by tracking scope, schedule, budget, risks, issues, dependencies, and resource utilization; implement corrective actions as needed to maintain project health and achieve desired outcomes. Communicate project progress, risks, issues, and recommendations to sponsors, governance committees, executive leadership, and stakeholders through regular status reporting, presentations, and project reviews. Facilitate and lead meetings, workshops, and stakeholder engagements to build consensus, resolve issues, manage change, and support successful project implementation and organizational adoption. Contribute to the continuous improvement of Project Management Office (PMO) processes, standards, methodologies, templates, and governance practices to enhance project delivery effectiveness, customer satisfaction, and organizational maturity. Assist with the development, maintenance, and enhancement of Project Management Office (PMO) methodologies, standards, templates, tools, and governance practices. Provide guidance, training, and mentoring to project team members, business stakeholders, and colleagues on project management principles, processes, and best practices. Support portfolio management activities by contributing to project intake, prioritization, reporting, resource planning, and project governance reviews. Research emerging project management methodologies, technologies, and industry trends and recommend improvements to organizational practices and project delivery capabilities. Prepare and maintain project documentation, records, presentations, and knowledge repositories to support audit, compliance, reporting, and operational needs. Represent the Project Management Office at workshops, conferences, professional development activities, and university events as requested.   Marginal Functions Participate in departmental, division, and university committees, task forces, and special initiatives as assigned to support institutional goals and continuous improvement efforts. Perform other related duties and special projects as assigned to support the mission, goals, and operational needs of Information Technology Services and the University.   Required Qualifications Master's and 1+ years of relevant experience or Bachelor's degree and 3+ years of relevant experience. Or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219. Certified Associate in Project Management (CAPM) or the ability to obtain CAPM preferred. Leadership: Leads cross-functional teams, builds consensus, and drives projects to successful completion. Communication: Effectively conveys information to technical and non-technical audiences through written, verbal, and presentation formats. Collaboration: Establishes productive relationships with stakeholders, project teams, vendors, and university leadership Problem Solving: Analyzes complex issues, identifies solutions, and recommends appropriate courses of action. Organization and Time Management: Effectively manages multiple priorities, deadlines, resources, and competing project demands. Project Management Methodologies: Knowledge of project management principles, best practices, and methodologies, including Agile, Waterfall, and hybrid approaches. Project Planning and Execution: Ability to develop and manage project charters, schedules, work plans, milestones, and deliverables throughout the project lifecycle. Risk and Change Management: Ability to identify, assess, mitigate, and monitor project risks, issues, dependencies, and change requests. Project Governance and Reporting: Ability to prepare project documentation, executive-level status reports, dashboards, and governance materials to support decision-making. Technology Project Delivery: Knowledge of information technology systems, software implementations, system integrations, cloud-based solutions, and enterprise applications to support successful project outcomes.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Instructor_JR103732": {
      "title": "Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nDepartment English & World Languages, Chair Compensation $54,300.00 Annual   General Description: This is a 9-month, non-tenure earning Instructor of English position in the Department of English and World Languages. Responsibilities include a 4/4 teaching load, or equivalent, plus service commensurate with the position.   The UNF Department of English and World Languages strongly values internship, student success, digital humanities, writing across the curriculum and writing in the disciplines. At UNF, the Department of English and World Languages prepares students to do exactly that. Across creative writing, literature, film, digital humanities, professional writing, and theater, students develop their voice alongside faculty who are working writers, scholars, and artists invested in where they are headed.   Supervisor: This position reports to the Department Chair, Dr. Tru Leverette Hall.   Working Hours: Varies   Supervision Exercised: This is not a supervisory role.   Required Licensure: N/A   Required Qualifications:  Master's degree in related field   Preferred Qualifications / Skills: The ideal candidate should have teaching and professional expertise in professional communication, technical writing, and writing studies. Significant factors for consideration will include demonstrated excellence in teaching and experience in writing across the curriculum. Additional factors include experience in coordinating internships and community outreach.   Anticipated Start Date: August 2, 2027   Additional Application Materials Required:   Applicants should be prepared to provide the following required documents:  Current curriculum vitae  Cover letter    Name, phone number, and email address of three professional references will be requested during the application review stage.    The selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts (and, as applicable, U.S. degree equivalency evaluations) documenting the conferral of their qualifying academic credentials by the date of hire.    Additional Requirements:   Applicants may be required to upload additional documents based on their responses to the Foreign Influence Review questions:  Passport (all pages including blank pages)  Form DS-160 (if ever submitted. If not, upload an explanation)    Application Review Date:  Initial review of applications will begin on October 13, 2027.   Job Posting Close Date:  Open until filled.    How to Apply:   Applicants must submit an online application that includes all required application documents. If you have any questions about this position, please contact Dr. Tru Leverette Hall at t.leverette.hall@unf.edu   About the Department:   The Department of English and World Languages at the University of North Florida offers courses in Composition & Rhetoric, Creative Writing, Digital Humanities, Film, Literature, Professional Writing, Theater, Spanish, French, and Chinese. The department offers two Bachelor of Arts programs in English: the B.A. in English and the B.A. in English with a Concentration in Creative Writing. Additionally, we offer a B.A. in Spanish and a B.A. in French and Francophone Studies. The English Graduate Program offers the M.A. in English and M.A. concentrations in Creative Writing and Composition and Rhetoric. The department also offers minors in Creative Writing, Film, Literature, Professional & Public Writing, Digital Humanities, Spanish, French, and Chinese. Our courses contribute to a range of interdisciplinary programs, including Africana Studies, English Education, Digital Humanities, and Gender Studies. The department is committed to providing high-quality instruction and fostering intellectual growth, preparing students for a wide range of professions that require strong communication and analytical skills. For more information about the Department of English and World Languages, visit:  https://www.unf.edu/coas/english/index.html     Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
