    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Assistant-Strength---Conditioning-Coach_JR103728": {
      "title": "Assistant Strength & Conditioning Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nDepartment Athletics, Strength & Conditioning Compensation $40,000.00 to Negotiable Annual   General Description/Primary Purpose: The Assistant Strength & Conditioning Coach's primary responsibility is the coaching and instruction of the strength and conditioning programs. Approximately 80% of the Assistant Coach's responsibility is dedicated to the instruction of strength and conditioning through weight room/facility training and classroom training through the use of video and other teaching techniques. Approximately 20% of the Assistant Coach's responsibility is working alongside coaching staff and other administrative duties. Job Functions: Assist in the coaching and instruction of the student-athletes in proper techniques and decision-making in strength and conditioning programs. Perform routine daily responsibilities related to the operation of the sports program. Work could include computer data-entry, routine record keeping, and compliance logs required by the NCAA. Assist in recruiting acceptable student-athletes for the UNF athletic program. Perform other duties as prescribed by the head coach. Could include clinic participation; scheduling; overseeing equipment needs; overseeing part-time staff or other related functions. Adheres to all institution, conference, and NCAA rules and regulations. Reports all known NCAA violations in accordance with institutional, conference, and NCAA policies and guidelines. Develop yearlong cycles designed for all UNF athletic teams, in conjunction with the goals set forth by the sport coaching staff and Strength and Conditioning Coach. Works directly with the sports medicine staff developing and monitoring rehabilitation programs and post-rehabilitation of student-athletes. Supervision Exercised : Assist in supervising volunteers, student assistants, etc. Supervision Received : Reports to the Head Coach   Required Qualifications Master's or Bachelor's degree and 2+ years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience pursuant to Fla. Stat. 112.219.  For more information about this position, please contact Brian Bert at brian.bert@unf.edu.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator   This position has been designated as a Campus Security Authority (CSA). This position has been designated as a CSA because it involves significant responsibility for student and campus activities and/or responsibility for campus security. As such, any person in this position must report to the University Police Department a crime or an incident that might be a crime that he/she becomes aware of. This position has a reporting requirement because the University believes that responsibility for students, campus activities and/or campus security will make the holder of this position someone members of the University community will see as an authority figure and someone to whom they can seek help. A CSA is not expected to investigate or determine whether a criminal incident actually took place. A CSA ’ s responsibility is a duty to report. All positions designated as CSAs are required to complete an online or in - person training session. For more information concerning training or CSA designations, please contact the Clery Act Compliance Manager at (904) 620-1423 or clery@unf.edu.   The holder of this position is responsible for any NCAA and Atlantic Sun Conference bylaws and guidelines that a member of the UNF Athletic Compliance Department provides in addition to all UNF regulations. The individual must also assure that NCAA, Conference and UNF regulations are followed to the best of their knowledge and any violations thereof are reported to UNF Athletic Compliance. Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Assistant-Director-of-the-School-of-Nursing---Business-Operations-and-Analytics_JR103722": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of the School of Nursing - Business Operations and Analytics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nDepartment School of Nursing Compensation $110,000.00 to Negotiable Annual   General Description/Primary Purpose The Assistant Director of the School of Nursing - Business Operations and Analytics reports directly to the Director of the School of Nursing. The Assistant Director provides strategic leadership and operational oversight to ensure the efficient, effective, and data-informed administration of the School's academic operations, business functions and strategic initiatives. This is a 12-month, tenure-track or tenured faculty appointment at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. The Assistant Director partners closely with the Director, the Assistant Director of Accreditation and Curriculum, Program Directors, faculty, and School of Nursing committees to execute the School's strategic priorities, optimize operational performance, and foster a culture of excellence, innovation, accountability, and continuous improvement. The Assistant Director leads the School's operational infrastructure, including business operations, faculty workload and resource management, operational analytics, strategic planning, project management, and organizational effectiveness. Through executive dashboards, key performance indicators, and operational reporting, the position provides data-informed recommendations that support strategic decision-making and continuous quality improvement. Working in close collaboration with the Assistant Director of Accreditation and Curriculum, this position ensures that operational processes, faculty resources, data collection, and systematic evaluation activities support ongoing compliance with CCNE accreditation standards, the AACN Essentials, university policies, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. Together, these complementary leaders ensure alignment between operational excellence, academic quality, strategic planning, and accreditation. Within the School's leadership structure, the Assistant Director of Business Operations and Analytics provides leadership for the business, operational, financial, and analytical functions of the School, while the Assistant Director of Accreditation and Curriculum provides leadership for curriculum, assessment, academic quality, faculty development, and accreditation. Together they support the Director in advancing the School's strategic vision and mission. The Assistant Director maintains an appropriate portfolio of teaching, scholarship, and service consistent with faculty appointment and administrative responsibilities. Operational Leadership & Administration Manage/coordinate day-to-day operational functions under the direction of the Director. Develop and improve operational systems, workflows, and administrative processes. Coordinate operational activities across academic programs, faculty, staff, simulation, clinical education, admissions, and university partners. Ensure operational readiness for each academic term. Promote organizational effectiveness and continuous process improvement. Business Operations & Resource Management Assist with operational budget development and monitoring. Coordinate/manage operational resource utilization consistent with Director-approved priorities and budget. Support operational management of grants and legislative funding initiatives. Administers/coordinates resources within approved budgets and priorities. Strategic Planning & Organizational Performance Partner with the Director to implement strategic priorities. Lead operational implementation of Director-approved strategic initiatives and organizational changes. Develop project plans, timelines, and accountability measures. Monitor progress toward strategic goals using performance metrics. Data Analytics & Business Intelligence Develop executive dashboards and key performance indicators (KPIs). Analyze enrollment, admissions, retention, graduation, NCLEX, faculty workload, simulation utilization, and other operational metrics. Prepare reports supporting accreditation, university leadership, and state reporting. Use predictive analytics to support enrollment, workforce planning, and resource allocation. Academic Operations Coordinate faculty workload, teaching assignments, and semester scheduling with the Director and Program Directors. Support recruitment, onboarding, and integration of full-time, adjunct, and OPS faculty. Coordinate operational processes supporting academic program delivery and student progression. Accreditation Support & Continuous Quality Improvement Collaborate with the Assistant Director of Accreditation and Curriculum to support CCNE accreditation, AACN Essentials, systematic evaluation, and continuous quality improvement. Support data collection, reporting, and implementation of operational improvements identified through assessment and accreditation activities. Leadership, Collaboration & Governance Collaborate with Program Directors, faculty, and School committees to implement strategic initiatives. Assist the Director with faculty recruitment, onboarding, workload planning, and provide workload/performance data and operational input to support Director-led annual evaluations. Promote a culture of collaboration, innovation, accountability, and operational excellence. Faculty Responsibilities Maintain an appropriate portfolio of teaching, scholarship, and service consistent with faculty appointment. Minimum Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in nursing (DNP, PhD, or other terminal nursing doctorate). Eligible for appointment as a tenure-track or tenured faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor or higher. Current, unencumbered RN license or eligibility for Florida licensure. Demonstrated experience in academic leadership, administration, or operational management. Strong analytical, organizational, financial, communication, and leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications Current Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) licensure and national certification. MBA or equivalent graduate degree in business, healthcare administration, public administration, or organizational leadership strongly preferred. Experience with budgeting, business operations, strategic planning, analytics, and project management. Knowledge of AACN Essentials, CCNE accreditation standards, and nursing program administration.   Supervisor: This position reports to the Director of the School of Nursing Anticipated Start Date: The position is expected to begin on January 4, 2027 Additional Application Materials Required: Applicants should be prepared to provide the following required documents: • Current curriculum vitae • Cover letter Name, phone number, and email address of three professional references will be requested during the application review stage. The selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts (and, as applicable, U.S. degree equivalency evaluations) documenting the conferral of their qualifying academic credentials by the date of hire. Additional Requirements: Applicants may be required to upload additional documents based on their responses to the Foreign Influence Review questions. • Passport (all pages including blank pages) and • Form DS-160 (if ever submitted. If not, upload an explanation) How to Apply: Applicants must submit an online application that includes all required application documents. If you have any questions about this position, please contact Dr. Judy Comeaux at jcomeaux@unf.edu Application Review Date: Initial review of applications will begin on November 2, 2026. Job Posting Close Date: Open until filled. About the Department: The School of Nursing offers a wide variety of programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Our programs have a community-based, population-focused curriculum corresponding to changes in healthcare delivery trends. The curriculum helps students understand community environments as well as nurturing and building relationships with community agencies. For more information about the School of Nursing, visit: https://www.unf.edu/brooks/nursing/index.html   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator Pursuant to Florida Statute 1010.35, this position requires additional information from all applicants seeking research or research-related positions prior to an interview or offer of employment. Applicants MUST fully complete the Foreign Influence Review section of their application. Additional documents (e.g., passport) may be required based on form responses.     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
