    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Part-Time-Adjunct-Professor--Music_JR103705": {
      "title": "Part-Time Adjunct Professor -Music",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nDepartment School of Music-OPS Compensation   General Description/Primary Purpose Part-time adjunct faculty position in the School of Music. Adjunct faculty are employed on a semester-by-semester basis, as needed, and are non-tenure-earning. Job Functions Position responsibilities include but are not limited to: Teach assigned course(s) in accordance with the approved syllabus and course schedule. Hold scheduled office hours with frequency and modality as negotiated with department chair. Marginal Functions Perform related duties as assigned. Working Hours: Part-time Work Schedule: Varies Supervision Exercised This is not a supervisory role. Required Licensure N/A Anticipated Start Date The position is expected to begin on Aug. 3, 2026. Compensation Adjunct faculty are paid a minimum of $1000 per credit hour. All exceptions must be approved by the Provost or his/her designee. Required Qualifications At a minimum, applicants must have earned a master’s degree in the hiring discipline or closely related field., or a bachelor’s degree in music with evidence of substantial experience and expertise in related field at the time of appointment. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching at the collegiate level. Experience teaching in a Learning Management System (LMS) platform, particularly the Canvas application. Experience teaching (insert name of preferred courses) at graduate level. Additional Application Materials Required Applicants should be prepared to provide the following required documents: Current curriculum vitae Cover letter Names, phone numbers, and email address of three professional references will be requested during the application review stage. The selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts (and, as applicable, U.S. degree equivalency evaluations) documenting the conferral of their qualifying academic credentials by the date of hire. Job Posting Close Date Open until filled. Note: Adjunct postings may close at any time without notice. How to Apply Applicants must submit an online application that includes all required application documents. If you have any questions about this position, please contact Barbara Cabe at (904) 620-2961 or barbara.cabe@unf.edu. About the Department The School of Music brings a focused commitment to excellence and the artistic and intellectual preparation of music students. Supporting the UNF Mission of being a hub for talent development, relevant research, and community engagement, the School of Music aims to attract talented students and provide them with a high level of professional musical training that is relevant to musicians pursuing musical careers in the 21st Century. The UNF School of Music faculty, excellent instructors evidenced by their innovative pedagogy, scholarship, and research in their respective fields, serve as artist-teachers working with students in large and small performing ensembles as well as through individual applied instruction. Our comprehensive program is complemented by the Ira M. Koger Eminent Scholar Chair in American Music that provides an additional focus on jazz. The School of Music continues to achieve national and international recognition as a distinguished comprehensive center for the study, creation, and research in music. The School of Music provides music majors and non-music majors alike the opportunity to develop their knowledge, understanding, and ability in all aspects of music at a level relevant and appropriate to their needs and interests, and to prepare music majors for careers as performers, teachers, composers, arrangers, and professionals in the music industry and its supporting fields. Our students experience transformational learning opportunities through international study abroad programs, interaction with world class guest artists and community-based performance and pedagogical programs. Our mission focuses on delivering outstanding academic and artistic education, equipping students for professional success in music. In showcasing the work of our students and faculty, we aspire to enrich community life and serve as a vital link between the University and the broader community. For more information about the School of Music visit: School of Music   Required Qualifications Temporary appointment extended to an expert in a specific field to give instruction in connection with an established program. The appointments are: for one (1) academic term at a time and possess no continuing contractual relationship with the University. May teach undergrad courses with Master's degree in specified discipline. Can be used for temporary (OPS) faculty titles only.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Small-Business-Consultant-OPS_JR103778": {
      "title": "Small Business Consultant OPS",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nDepartment Small Business Development Center (SBDC)-OPS Compensation $30.00 Hourly     Required Qualifications General Description The Small Business Consultant provides consulting, training, and outreach services to prospective and existing small business owners throughout the Florida SBDC at UNF's 18-county service area. The consultant reports to the Assistant Director or above and works collaboratively with university personnel, community stakeholders, economic development organizations, and funding partners to support the growth and success of small businesses. The consultant delivers one-on-one business consulting, educational programs, and community outreach activities while assisting clients with business planning, financial management, and access to capital opportunities. Job Functions Consulting Services Provide consulting services to prospective, startup, and existing Florida small businesses. Assist clients with activities related to starting, managing, and growing a small business. Assist clients in developing, implementing, and evaluating business plans and growth strategies. Conduct financial analysis and develop financial projections, cash flow forecasts, and budgets. Deliver targeted Florida SBDC programs and services as assigned, including microenterprise and specialty assistance programs. Maintain accurate client records and activity reporting in required management information systems. Collaborate with internal and external partners to ensure effective delivery of services. Access to Capital Assistance Assist clients in identifying, evaluating, and accessing appropriate sources of capital, including conventional bank financing, SBA loan programs, microloans, community development financial institutions (CDFIs), grants, and alternative financing options. Conduct loan readiness assessments and assist clients with financial statement review, cash flow analysis, debt service evaluation, and financial projections. Assist clients in preparing financing packages and supporting documentation required by lenders or investors. Educate clients on financing requirements and available funding resources. Develop and maintain relationships with lenders, financial institutions, investors, and other capital providers throughout the service area. Support clients in preparing for meetings with lenders and capital providers. Training Develop educational content and training materials for entrepreneurs and small business owners. Deliver workshops, webinars, and training programs independently and in collaboration with partners and stakeholders. Identify opportunities to expand educational programming and increase engagement with existing and prospective clients. Present on topics related to business planning, finance, access to capital, and small business management. Outreach Conduct outreach activities to educate clients, partners, and stakeholders on Florida SBDC services and impact. Represent the Florida SBDC at UNF at community, business, and economic development events. Assist in identifying and securing resources that support expansion of SBDC programs and services. Develop and maintain relationships with community organizations, stakeholders, resource partners, and funding entities. Serve on boards, committees, or task forces as assigned. Supervision and Administration Foster an engaged and collaborative work environment. Provide supervision and guidance to assigned OPS staff, student assistants, training assistants, and consulting coordinators as assigned. Ensure compliance with Florida SBDC Network, UNF, and funding partner requirements. Meet assigned program deliverables, performance measures, and annual KPIs. Assist with interpretation and implementation of departmental policies and procedures. Travel Travel throughout the 18-county service area as required. Attend state, regional, and national professional development events as assigned. Attend occasional early morning, evening, and after-hours business events and meetings. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Finance, Accounting, Economics, Management, Entrepreneurship, or a related field. Minimum of five (5) years of professional experience in one or more of the following areas: Commercial lending Small business banking Business finance Financial analysis Capital access consulting Business ownership Economic development Small business consulting Related business advisory services Demonstrated experience assisting small businesses with financial management, business planning, and access to capital. Experience analyzing financial statements, cash flow, profitability, and financial projections. Strong written, verbal, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and Google applications, virtual meeting platforms, and CRM systems. Ability to work independently and manage multiple priorities. Valid driver's license and ability to travel throughout the service area. Preferred Qualifications Experience with SBA lending programs, including SBA 7(a), 504, and Microloan Programs. Existing relationships with commercial lenders, community lenders, and capital providers. Experience providing consulting or advisory services to entrepreneurs and small business owners. Experience delivering business training workshops and public presentations. Knowledge of Florida's small business ecosystem and economic development resources. Previous experience working with a Small Business Development Center, economic development organization, financial institution, or entrepreneurial support organization. Marginal Functions During declared campus emergencies, this position may be required to perform specific job-related duties at a designated off-campus location or place of residence and perform other duties as assigned.   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
    },
    "https://unf.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/unfjobs/job/Jacksonville-FL/Instructor_JR103733": {
      "title": "Instructor of Accounting & Taxation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nDepartment Accounting & Finance, Chair Compensation $95,000.00 Annual   General Description: This is a 9-month, non-tenure earning, Instructor of Accounting & Taxation position in the Department of Accounting & Finance. Position responsibilities include teaching a 4/4 load (four courses in the fall, and four courses in the spring), or its equivalent. In addition, this position includes service responsibilities to the department and college (committee work, mentoring students, etc.).   Supervisor : This position reports to the Department Chair.   Working Hours: Varies   Supervision Exercised: No   Required Licensure: N/A   Required Qualifications: A master’s degree from an accredited institution in accounting, taxation, or a closely related field OR a C.P.A. license with significant professional experience Demonstrated commitment to effective teaching and student success A record of academic and/or professional engagement consistent with the standards and expectations of an AACSB-accredited college of business    Preferred Qualifications / Skills: Professional certification or licenses such as C.P.A., C.M.A., C.I.A., etc. Doctoral degree or associated coursework in accounting, taxation, or related fields Experience teaching accounting or taxation at the undergraduate level Experience teaching accounting or taxation in a professional setting   Anticipated Start Date: December 16, 2026   Additional Application Materials Required: Applicants should be prepared to provide the following required documents: Current curriculum vitae Cover letter   Name, phone number, and email address of three professional references will be requested during the application review stage.   The selected candidate will be required to submit official transcripts (and, as applicable, U.S. degree equivalency evaluations) documenting the conferral of their qualifying academic credentials by the date of hire.   Additional Requirements: Applicants may be required to upload additional documents based on their responses to the Foreign Influence Review questions. Passport (all pages including blank pages) and Form DS-160 (if ever submitted. If not, upload an explanation)   How to Apply: Applicants must submit an online application that includes all required application documents. If you have any questions about this position, please contact Elise Fellows, Office Manager, Department of Accounting & Finance, at (904) 620-2633 or elise.fellows@unf.edu .   Application Review Date: October 15, 2026   Job Posting Close Date: Open until filled.   About Department: The Coggin College of Business is an AACSB-accredited college serving approximately 3,500 undergraduate and graduate students and is committed to academic excellence and student success. In August 2026, Coggin opened a new building expansion, providing additional space and resources for students, faculty, academic programs, collaboration, and engagement with the business community.   The Department of Accounting & Finance is one of four academic departments within the Coggin College of Business and is home to undergraduate programs in Accounting, Finance, and Financial Planning. The department also offers the Master of Accountancy, the M.S. in Accounting Data Analytics, and the M.S. in FinTech. The department maintains strong relationships with the business communities in Jacksonville and Northeast Florida.   For more information about the Coggin College of Business programs, centers, faculty, and strategic initiatives, visit https://www.unf.edu/coggin/about/index.html .   Statement(s) of Understanding This position requires a background check. In conjunction with the University's policy, this position may also require a credit check. The holder of this position is designated as a “Responsible Employee” pursuant to their role under Title IX. Therefore, the incumbent must promptly report allegations of sexual misconduct, sexual violence, and child sexual abuse by or against any student, employee, contractor, or visitor to the University’s Title IX Administrator or any divisional Title IX Coordinator     Equal Opportunity The University of North Florida (UNF) is committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for all who interact in our community. In building this environment, we strive to attract students, faculty and staff from a variety of cultures, backgrounds and life experiences. The University of North Florida does not commit or permit discrimination or harassment on the basis of genetic information, race, color, religion, age, sex, disability, marital status, national origin, or veteran status in any educational, employment, social, recreational program or activity that it offers. In addition, UNF will not commit or permit retaliation against an individual who reports discrimination or harassment or an individual who cooperates in an investigation of an alleged violation of university regulation. Carnegie UNF is a Carnegie Community Engaged Institution. This designation celebrates the University’s collaboration with community partners from the local to the global level. It reflects UNF’s mission to contribute to the public good and prepare educated, engaged citizens."
